{"id":"ux-accessibility","title":"UI/UX: accessibility","subject":"UI/UX design","label":"UI/UX design","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":181,"duration":180.54,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":483,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":15.885},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":15.885,"end":49.265},{"id":"explain2","title":"Rules","start":49.265,"end":94.095},{"id":"example","title":"Example","start":94.095,"end":119.615},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":119.615,"end":129.175},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":129.175,"end":137.725},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Mistakes","start":137.725,"end":158.115},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":158.115,"end":180.54}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.52,"text":"Have you ever tried to read a message in bright sunlight and the words disappeared?","w":[0.54,0.7,0.84,1.06,1.34,1.44,1.62,1.68,2.02,2.18,2.48,3.28,3.4,3.52,3.88]},{"s":0,"a":4.97,"b":8.13,"text":"Or watched a video on a noisy bus with no captions?","w":[5.04,5.2,5.56,5.66,6.14,6.24,6.36,6.74,7.16,7.34,7.5]},{"s":0,"a":8.58,"b":15.46,"text":"I'm Kora. Today we look at accessibility in UI and UX, designing so everyone can use your product.","w":[8.66,8.86,9.72,10.18,10.34,10.52,10.62,11.4,11.64,12.08,12.28,13.22,13.72,13.96,14.34,14.62,14.76,14.96]},{"s":1,"a":16.31,"b":20.39,"text":"Accessibility means you design so people with disabilities can use your product.","w":[16.36,17.1,17.34,17.5,17.98,18.18,18.46,18.62,19.28,19.56,19.7,19.88]},{"s":1,"a":20.69,"b":23.43,"text":"This includes people who are blind or have low vision.","w":[20.7,20.92,21.36,21.66,21.8,21.96,22.44,22.56,22.8,23.04]},{"s":1,"a":23.73,"b":27.81,"text":"It also includes people who are colour blind, deaf, or hard of hearing.","w":[23.8,23.94,24.24,24.66,24.92,25.08,25.26,25.6,26.46,26.9,27.06,27.28,27.38]},{"s":1,"a":28.11,"b":32.19,"text":"Some have limited movement. Others find reading or concentration hard.","w":[28.24,28.56,28.78,29.14,30.12,30.44,30.74,31.08,31.22,31.92]},{"s":1,"a":32.49,"b":38.36,"text":"The World Health Organization estimates about one in six people worldwide live with a significant disability.","w":[32.52,32.66,33.04,33.38,34.18,34.66,35.08,35.32,35.5,35.76,36.12,36.78,37.02,37.18,37.24,37.78]},{"s":1,"a":38.66,"b":42,"text":"That is a huge group, so this matters for every designer.","w":[38.68,38.92,39.04,39.18,39.56,40.12,40.28,40.5,40.92,41.22,41.46]},{"s":1,"a":42.3,"b":48.84,"text":"Accessible design also helps everyone. Captions help in a noisy bus. Strong contrast helps in bright sunlight.","w":[42.38,42.88,43.36,43.68,43.94,44.84,45.32,45.56,45.66,45.72,46.06,46.94,47.32,47.88,48.14,48.24,48.52]},{"s":2,"a":49.69,"b":54.25,"text":"The main guide is the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines, WCAG.","w":[49.74,49.88,50.16,50.58,50.68,50.82,51.1,51.62,52.3,53.22]},{"s":2,"a":54.55,"b":57.57,"text":"These rules are practical. They remove common barriers.","w":[54.55,54.82,55.14,55.26,56.16,56.32,56.68,57]},{"s":2,"a":57.87,"b":64.51,"text":"For normal text, WCAG level double A asks for a contrast ratio of at least four point five to one.","w":[57.9,58.08,58.42,59.42,60.26,60.56,60.9,61.48,61.76,61.92,62,62.5,62.98,63.08,63.18,63.42,63.68,63.9,64.16,64.36]},{"s":2,"a":64.81,"b":69.83,"text":"Never use colour alone to give meaning. Add an icon or words to a red error.","w":[64.94,65.32,65.5,65.88,66.22,66.34,66.54,67.48,67.64,67.88,68.34,68.5,68.88,69.06,69.16,69.5]},{"s":2,"a":70.13,"b":74.93,"text":"Give images text alternatives, called alt text, so a screen reader can describe them.","w":[70.16,70.46,70.92,71.3,72.06,72.42,72.62,73.34,73.52,73.6,73.9,74.18,74.34,74.76]},{"s":2,"a":75.23,"b":76.62,"text":"Add captions to video.","w":[75.32,75.52,76.08,76.2]},{"s":2,"a":76.92,"b":81,"text":"Make touch targets big enough to tap, about forty four to forty eight pixels.","w":[77,77.28,77.6,78.04,78.24,78.52,78.66,78.98,79.26,79.56,79.86,80.02,80.3,80.48]},{"s":2,"a":81.3,"b":85.05,"text":"Use clear labels on form fields, not only placeholder text.","w":[81.42,81.68,82,82.42,82.56,82.86,83.58,83.86,84.1,84.64]},{"s":2,"a":85.35,"b":86.78,"text":"Let text be made larger.","w":[85.42,85.64,85.98,86.1,86.32]},{"s":2,"a":87.08,"b":89,"text":"Make everything reachable by keyboard.","w":[87.14,87.48,87.94,88.34,88.52]},{"s":2,"a":89.3,"b":93.67,"text":"Each rule removes one barrier, and together they open your product to everyone.","w":[89.36,89.6,89.98,90.52,90.68,91.48,91.6,92.04,92.26,92.46,92.6,93.08,93.24]},{"s":3,"a":94.52,"b":97.89,"text":"Imagine a form shows errors only by turning the box red.","w":[94.62,95.02,95.14,95.48,95.88,96.38,96.62,96.82,97.16,97.26,97.58]},{"s":3,"a":98.19,"b":103.71,"text":"Step one, ask what carries the meaning here. Only colour does, so some users will miss it.","w":[98.28,98.72,99.44,99.68,99.86,100.24,100.36,100.66,101.36,101.66,102.04,102.32,102.56,102.88,103.18,103.36,103.62]},{"s":3,"a":104.01,"b":108.07,"text":"A person who cannot tell those colours apart may not notice the change.","w":[104.08,104.16,104.6,104.76,105.18,105.44,105.7,106.08,106.88,107.1,107.32,107.64,107.76]},{"s":3,"a":108.37,"b":112.62,"text":"Step two, fix it with an icon and a message such as Enter a valid email.","w":[108.46,108.76,109.5,109.76,109.84,109.98,110.18,110.6,110.74,110.82,111.2,111.42,111.62,111.9,111.96,112.26]},{"s":3,"a":112.92,"b":115.21,"text":"Also put a clear label above the field.","w":[113.02,113.38,113.54,113.7,114.06,114.52,114.8,114.92]},{"s":3,"a":115.51,"b":119.19,"text":"That one change helps screen reader users and sighted users too.","w":[115.6,115.96,116.18,116.56,116.86,117.24,117.62,118.06,118.24,118.64,118.96]},{"s":4,"a":120.04,"b":123.14,"text":"A chart uses only red and green to show bad and good.","w":[120.14,120.26,120.64,121,121.28,121.56,121.7,122.04,122.2,122.5,122.82,122.92]},{"s":4,"a":123.44,"b":126,"text":"Who may struggle, and what is one fix?","w":[123.44,123.62,123.84,124.68,124.82,125.04,125.28,125.52]},{"s":4,"a":126.45,"b":128.75,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[126.5,126.84,127.14,127.28,127.58,128.28,128.48]},{"s":5,"a":129.6,"b":134.63,"text":"People with red and green colour blindness may struggle, because colour alone carries the meaning.","w":[129.64,129.96,130.2,130.52,130.68,131.02,131.32,131.8,132,132.88,133.22,133.58,133.98,134.34,134.44]},{"s":5,"a":134.93,"b":137.3,"text":"Add labels, patterns, or icons.","w":[135,135.2,135.82,136.48,136.74]},{"s":6,"a":138.15,"b":142.88,"text":"Mistake one is treating accessibility as an extra at the end. Build it in from the start.","w":[138.18,138.7,138.84,139,139.34,140.1,140.22,140.38,140.72,140.82,141,141.72,142,142.12,142.26,142.4,142.5]},{"s":6,"a":143.18,"b":151.02,"text":"Mistake two is light grey text and tiny tap targets. Use stronger contrast and larger targets, about forty four pixels or more.","w":[143.24,143.7,144.02,144.18,144.46,144.72,145.14,145.3,145.64,145.9,146.88,147.06,147.56,148.18,148.3,148.66,149.32,149.62,149.9,150.16,150.58,150.7]},{"s":6,"a":151.32,"b":157.69,"text":"Mistake three is using images of text or colour alone. Use real text and add labels or icons.","w":[151.38,151.88,152.22,152.4,152.74,153.16,153.3,153.7,153.86,154.2,155.12,155.36,155.64,156.12,156.32,156.5,156.94,157.18]},{"s":7,"a":158.54,"b":162.47,"text":"Accessibility means designing for disabled people, and it helps everyone.","w":[158.58,159.36,159.64,160.2,160.36,160.82,161.42,161.56,161.66,162]},{"s":7,"a":162.77,"b":167.69,"text":"WCAG gives clear rules, like strong contrast and keyboard access.","w":[163.12,163.92,164.24,164.58,165.24,165.5,166,166.6,166.76,167.18]},{"s":7,"a":167.99,"b":172.02,"text":"Add alt text, captions, labels, and large tap targets.","w":[168.12,168.44,168.66,169.26,170.08,170.62,170.8,171.2,171.48]},{"s":7,"a":172.32,"b":176.12,"text":"Top tip: test your design with a keyboard and with colour turned off.","w":[172.38,172.68,173.44,173.68,173.84,174.24,174.4,174.48,175.06,175.16,175.36,175.72,176.02]},{"s":7,"a":176.42,"b":179.94,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and make every screen welcoming.","w":[176.46,176.72,177.24,177.42,178.24,178.38,178.76,179.06,179.48]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday barriers","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Bright sunlight: words disappear"},{"at":4.87,"kind":"text","text":"Noisy bus: video without captions"},{"at":8.48,"kind":"term","text":"Accessibility (UI/UX)","detail":"Design so everyone can use your product"}]},{"at":16.06,"heading":"Accessibility includes","items":[{"at":16.21,"kind":"term","text":"Accessibility","detail":"Design so people with disabilities can use your product"},{"at":20.59,"kind":"text","text":"Blind or low vision"},{"at":23.63,"kind":"text","text":"Colour blind, deaf, or hard of hearing"},{"at":28.01,"kind":"text","text":"Limited movement; reading or concentration hard"}]},{"at":32.24,"heading":"Why it matters","items":[{"at":32.39,"kind":"text","text":"WHO: about 1 in 6 people have significant disability"},{"at":38.56,"kind":"text","text":"Huge group: matters for every designer"},{"at":42.2,"kind":"text","text":"Also helps everyone: captions, contrast"}]},{"at":49.44,"heading":"WCAG rules","items":[{"at":49.59,"kind":"term","text":"WCAG","detail":"Web Content Accessibility Guidelines"},{"at":54.45,"kind":"text","text":"Practical rules remove common barriers"},{"at":57.77,"kind":"formula","text":"AA normal text contrast: 4.5:1 min"},{"at":64.71,"kind":"text","text":"Never use colour alone; add icon or words"},{"at":70.03,"kind":"term","text":"Alt text","detail":"Text alternative so screen reader describes images"}]},{"at":74.98,"heading":"More WCAG rules","items":[{"at":75.13,"kind":"text","text":"Add captions to video"},{"at":76.82,"kind":"text","text":"Touch targets 44 to 48 px"},{"at":81.2,"kind":"text","text":"Clear labels on form fields, not just placeholders"},{"at":85.25,"kind":"text","text":"Let text be made larger"},{"at":86.98,"kind":"text","text":"Everything reachable by keyboard"}]},{"at":94.27,"heading":"Error example","items":[{"at":94.42,"kind":"text","text":"Form errors shown only by red box"},{"at":98.09,"kind":"text","text":"Step 1: only colour carries meaning"},{"at":103.91,"kind":"text","text":"Some users cannot see the colour change"},{"at":108.27,"kind":"text","text":"Step 2: add icon + 'Enter a valid email'"}]},{"at":112.67,"heading":"Fix the form","items":[{"at":112.82,"kind":"text","text":"Add clear label above the field"},{"at":115.41,"kind":"text","text":"Helps screen reader and sighted users"}]},{"at":119.61,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":119.61,"kind":"question","text":"A chart uses only red and green to show bad and good. Who may struggle, and what is one fix?"}]},{"at":129.35,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":129.5,"kind":"text","text":"Red-green colour blindness: colour alone carries meaning"},{"at":134.83,"kind":"text","text":"Fix: add labels, patterns or icons"}]},{"at":137.9,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":138.05,"kind":"wrong","text":"Accessibility as an extra at the end"},{"at":143.08,"kind":"wrong","text":"Light grey text and tiny tap targets"}]},{"at":151.07,"heading":"More mistakes","items":[{"at":151.22,"kind":"wrong","text":"Images of text or colour alone"}]},{"at":158.29,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":158.44,"kind":"text","text":"Accessibility: design for disabled people; helps everyone"},{"at":162.67,"kind":"text","text":"WCAG: strong contrast and keyboard access"},{"at":167.89,"kind":"text","text":"Add alt text, captions, labels, large tap targets"},{"at":172.22,"kind":"tip","text":"Top tip: test with a keyboard and with colour turned off"},{"at":176.32,"kind":"text","text":"Keep practising; make every screen welcoming"}]}],"check":{"at":129,"seconds":10,"question":"A chart uses only red and green to show bad and good. Who may struggle, and what is one fix?","answer":"People with red and green colour blindness may struggle; add labels, patterns or icons."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}